1
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,140
Brighten up the room and
try stepping back a little.

2
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:24,260
If you're broke, come on over to my place.

3
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,960
I'm broke too, but don't you worry.

4
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:32,820
Look at the blue sky!

5
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:36,320
White clouds.

6
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:42,820
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,920
If you're out of work,
come on over to my place.

8
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:04,560
I've got nothing either,
but don't you worry.

9
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:12,100
Even the steel cluster burning today,

10
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:18,260
it'll all work out somehow, eventually.

11
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:23,520
You understand, right? Got it, got it.

12
00:01:24,010 --> 00:01:27,420
Once you get it, follow me without a word.

13
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:43,680
Ryo-san's long day

14
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:31,300
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

15
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:33,160
Sorry!

16
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:36,380
I am apologizing, Chief!

17
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:40,500
Idiot! Hurry up and pay the bill!

18
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:43,500
I didn't expect such a trap.

19
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:44,060
Damn it,

20
00:02:44,110 --> 00:02:47,840
I knew it was strange for the Chief to
go out of his way to give me a present.

21
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:52,000
Ugh, guess I'll get up.

22
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:54,160
It's not like the Chief woke me up.

23
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:56,840
I got up because I was too hungry.

24
00:02:58,180 --> 00:03:00,340
Let's see, any food...?

25
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:05,340
There's rice balls and natto,

26
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:10,220
I don't remember when I bought them, but I must
have grabbed them drunk at the convenience store.

27
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:14,420
What's this smell?

28
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:23,000
Best before: July 5, 1999

29
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:26,640
An onigiri from the 20th century,
no wonder it's rotten.

30
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:29,600
The natto's fine, right?

31
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:32,352
This one's from the Showa era?

32
00:03:32,402 --> 00:03:35,460
B-but... it's p-pitch black!

33
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:38,449
I-it's a fossilized natto.

34
00:03:38,499 --> 00:03:41,080
There's no way I can eat this. Damn it.

35
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:44,980
Now that I know I can't eat it,
I'm even hungrier.

36
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:51,720
I'm so hungry I don't even
have the energy to pedal.

37
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,360
Mochi mochi!

38
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,360
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

39
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:56,540
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

40
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:05,420
!

41
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:07,300
Granny, go save that dog!

42
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:11,200
Ugh, I'm heading to work now,
and I'm gonna be late...

43
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:11,860
Granny!

44
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:15,720
If I'm late, the Chief will...

45
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:19,400
And I'm starving, too...

46
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:20,230
Yeah,

47
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:23,800
Damn it! Move, you brats!

48
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:26,160
Eeeeeeeh!

49
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,320
Whoa!

50
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:36,340
Eeeeeeh

51
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:41,140
Aaaaaah

52
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:42,940
Iiiiiiii

53
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:45,280
Eeeeeeh

54
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:50,520
See ya.

55
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:51,700
Thanks.

56
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:54,480
Good for you, little doggy.

57
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,760
The dog's gone.

58
00:04:58,080 --> 00:05:01,340
After all that work, I'm even hungrier.

59
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:03,660
I can't get any strength.

60
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:09,600
Hey, it followed me after all?

61
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:12,620
On top of being late,
if I bring a stray dog along too...

62
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:14,600
What's the Chief gonna say?

63
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:19,040
Enough already, seriously.

64
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,380
Good morning, senpai.

65
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:38,340
Chief Ohara, after all the trouble
we went to giving him an alarm clock!

66
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:41,080
He was furious, shouting,
"What's the meaning of this lateness?"

67
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:44,940
Furious So where's the Chief? In the back?

68
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,700
He went out to the squad leaders' meeting.

69
00:05:47,420 --> 00:05:49,720
I see. Phew, that's a relief.

70
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:53,540
It's not fine!
This is your tenth day in a row being late!

71
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:56,760
Well, what could I do?
On the way here today...

72
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:01,100
Archer followed me all the way here,
the little mutt.

73
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,620
This stray was drowning in the river,
so I saved him.

74
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:10,520
So that's why he's so attached to you.

75
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:11,440
Yeah, well.

76
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:14,760
Aren't you a cute little doggy?
Want a biscuit or something?

77
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:17,080
Hand over some food, will you?

78
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:21,060
There's none left.

79
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,080
So you were hungry

80
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:32,460
Look at you, eating the whole box.
How resourceful.

81
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,440
I haven't eaten a thing
since this morning either.

82
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:40,320
I'm going out on patrol and
grabbing breakfast on the way.

83
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:44,240
So, can you lend me a thousand yen?

84
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:47,720
I already borrowed a
thousand yen from Reiko.

85
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:52,180
With this, I'll get a beef bowl, tofu on the side,
miso soup, an egg, and pickles, please!

86
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:57,800
Hehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehe

87
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:01,100
Got a little carried away.
Not watching where I was going.

88
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:04,200
Hey, the thousand yen
I borrowed from Reiko...

89
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:05,400
Found it!

90
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:09,700
Hey, wait!

91
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:12,060
How far is it going to fly?

92
00:07:13,420 --> 00:07:14,880
On top of the building!

93
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:17,980
Okay, stay right there.

94
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:19,560
I'm coming to get you now.

95
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:22,160
My precious money for food!

96
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:23,460
Catch it!

97
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:26,980
Are you fucking with me?

98
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:28,140
This bastard!

99
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:30,080
Get back here, you!

100
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:31,580
Money, money, money!

101
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:32,640
Whoa!

102
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:38,480
Damn it! I won't let you get away!

103
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:41,080
Behold my awesome leap!

104
00:07:41,820 --> 00:07:43,140
Yes! I did it!

105
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:50,000
Dammit! I'm gonna catch you no matter what!

106
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:56,940
Whoa! Into the cooldown!

107
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:09,960


108
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:11,760
It's a printout.

109
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:16,720
Alright, then. Extra-large, extra-broth,
with egg miso soup and pickles.

110
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:19,560
Excuse me, sir.
Could I please have your meal ticket?

111
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,020
Right.

112
00:08:22,060 --> 00:08:24,000
If I just force it in, it might fit.

113
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:27,020
Damn it, it won't fit!

114
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:34,440
Are you all right?

115
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:35,880
Back on!

116
00:08:39,780 --> 00:08:41,220
I'm borrowing the police!

117
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:46,480
Think you can catch up on a bicycle?

118
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,120
What?

119
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:51,820
Trying to escape from me?
You're a thousand years too early.

120
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:52,340
Oh my.

121
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:53,020
Damn it.

122
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:55,120
This bastard.

123
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:57,360
But you're naive.

124
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,340
Sorry about that.

125
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:02,820
No way.

126
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,260
Easy as pie.

127
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:15,060
Watch out!

128
00:09:15,060 --> 00:09:17,120
Damn it!

129
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:18,060
I won't let you go!

130
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:24,760
Careful!

131
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:28,620
I'm so hungry I can't
put any strength into it.

132
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:32,220
But don't think you can
escape from me, Ryotsu!

133
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:33,280
Yes!

134
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,800
Aaaaaah! Alright, yeah!

135
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:43,880
Well, then...

136
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:54,240
Ugh, no good, I'm so hungry I can't move another inch.
Senpai, that was quite the feat.

137
00:09:54,940 --> 00:10:01,340
Ryo-chan, you're actually useful for once If only you hadn't been so hungry,
you could've thrown the criminal and arrested him too.

138
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:03,514
Hey, we're heading out from Kameari Park.

139
00:10:03,564 --> 00:10:06,800
One home-cooked meal, extra large portion.
Hurry up!

140
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:09,973
Senpai, we have business at the station now,

141
00:10:10,023 --> 00:10:11,440
so could you mind the box?

142
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:14,720
I'm not going anywhere anyway.
I can't take a single step.

143
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:18,940
What, you're still here?

144
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:20,980
Hungry?

145
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:25,120
My hunger comes first. Go away.

146
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:36,720
Then just chew on your shoes.

147
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:45,540
Who told you to chew on my leg?

148
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:51,200
You bastard, I saved your life!

149
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:52,960
Here you go.

150
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,340
That's a lot faster than usual, isn't it?

151
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:58,920
But you said it was urgent!

152
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,820
Even so, that's too fast.

153
00:11:00,820 --> 00:11:03,000
Surely this isn't something
a customer left behind?

154
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:06,080
No way, it's freshly fried, I swear!

155
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:08,100
Getting so defensive is what's suspicious.

156
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:09,640
Come on, give me a break.

157
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:11,920
Still,

158
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:13,660
this is awfully thin, isn't it.

159
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:15,840
Is there meat in this?

160
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:17,780
There is, plenty of it!

161
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:20,220
At this point, it's a masterful art.

162
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:22,200
I can see right through it.

163
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:23,900
It's always like this.

164
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:25,560
Ryo-san, the bill.

165
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:27,340
Don't tell me it's on credit.

166
00:11:27,340 --> 00:11:29,100
That's a terrible thing to say!

167
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:30,540
I've got the money, don't worry.

168
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:32,720
Here you go. Keep the change.

169
00:11:33,700 --> 00:11:34,320
Thanks for your business.

170
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:35,800
So, what's this?

171
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:37,680
It's a thousand-yen bill, obviously!

172
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:39,240
It's a bit dirty, though.

173
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,260
Dirty?

174
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:42,520
With this,
I can't even tell if it's a bill or what.

175
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:44,200
Well, try washing it clean.

176
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,380
It's definitely genuine.

177
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:48,600
If it's not a real bill,
I won't stand for it.

178
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:49,300
It's fine.

179
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:51,860
It's a genuine thousand-yen bill.

180
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:55,640
Now I can finally get some food.

181
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:56,940
Whoa...

182
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:22,840
Grrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrr...

183
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:25,520
My money's dwindling so fast,
my eyes are going blurry!

184
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:26,920
Damn it!

185
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:45,280
If the Chief saw me doing this,
who knows what he'd say.

186
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:54,380
I think there was a scene in an
old movie where someone ate a shoe.

187
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:57,080
Maybe it's not so bad after all.

188
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:02,300
Shoes are made of cowhide too, after all.

189
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:04,320
It's like beef jerky.

190
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:10,620
If I simmer it thoroughly,
I bet it'll turn back into beef.

191
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:15,420
Yes, yes, this is looking good.

192
00:13:16,620 --> 00:13:19,519
Mm, it's finally starting to look like meat.

193
00:13:19,569 --> 00:13:21,700
This might be sirloin.

194
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:26,820
I'll grill it while
brushing it with soy sauce.

195
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,240
Mm, it smells great.

196
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:37,600
What a feast. Itadakimasu.

197
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:40,480
It's a bit hard to cut.

198
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:43,340
Well then, how does it taste?

199
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:47,340
It's still kind of tough.

200
00:13:47,340 --> 00:13:48,980
It has quite a chewy texture.

201
00:13:48,980 --> 00:13:52,040
But the more I chew, the more the flavor...

202
00:13:58,100 --> 00:14:00,140
It was synthetic leather.

203
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:03,840
Damn, I'm starving.

204
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:05,860
Oh well, there's no helping it.

205
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:08,760
Guess I'll tidy up to take my mind off it.

206
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,880
But this is harder than it looks.

207
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:17,600
Every little move I make
just gnaws at my stomach.

208
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:19,140
Excuse me sorry.

209
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:23,480
I'd like to ask you something about Sunday.

210
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:25,740
What did you say, road?

211
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:28,120
I'm sorry.

212
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:30,320
Damn it.

213
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:34,060
When you're too hungry, you get irritable.

214
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:36,400
Stay calm, stay calm.

215
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:40,020
Geez, what a persistent bastard.

216
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:43,200
Mind if I eat my lunch here?

217
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:45,240
It's that greedy old hag.

218
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:47,960
I'm busy here. Do whatever you want.

219
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:49,280
Thanks, thanks.

220
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:51,660
Here we go.

221
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:55,420
You just feel more settled eating under a roof,
don't you.

222
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:57,560
Well, good for you.

223
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:04,260
Hey, what are you doing?

224
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:08,194
Isn't it obvious?
It's sukiyaki, you know. You...

225
00:15:08,244 --> 00:15:11,540
I have to carry heavy loads,
so I need to keep my strength up.

226
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:13,880
Don't do that in the police box!

227
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:18,680
Are you hungry already, officer?

228
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:21,960
I haven't eaten a thing since this morning.

229
00:15:22,010 --> 00:15:24,200
Still, that looks delicious.

230
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:26,920
You like sukiyaki too, officer?

231
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:29,080
Love sukiyaki, love it!

232
00:15:29,580 --> 00:15:31,560
So, I guess watching you
eat is good enough, then.

233
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:34,780
Don't tease me like that!

234
00:15:34,780 --> 00:15:36,600
This is just one serving.

235
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:39,240
I'm starving.

236
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:41,660
Damn it, this is so frustrating!

237
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:44,540
So you want to fight?

238
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:47,820
You son of a bitch!

239
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,880
Oops, I made a mess again.

240
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:59,300
Officer,
would you like to have a little meat too?

241
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:00,980
Yes, yes, I'll eat!

242
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:01,920
I'll eat!

243
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:11,400
You bastard! I'm not forgiving you anymore!

244
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:13,800
Get back here!

245
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:18,820
It's all your fault I've
had to go through this!

246
00:16:19,460 --> 00:16:20,600
Get back here!

247
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:27,640
What?

248
00:16:32,180 --> 00:16:34,320
A jumbo omelet rice for twenty people

249
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:37,700
If you can eat it in twenty minutes,
you win a 5,000-yen prize.

250
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,920
Wow, well done, Norako!

251
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,660
With my empty stomach like this right now,

252
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:44,800
Twenty servings of omelet rice?
Five minutes, no problem.

253
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:50,840
That looks good, doesn't it?

254
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:53,900
If you go over twenty minutes,
even by a second,

255
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:57,600
even if you finish it, you'll still
have to pay for the twenty servings.

256
00:16:58,160 --> 00:17:00,920
Fine by me.
Make it five minutes if you like.

257
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:02,580
You must be joking.

258
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:04,760
Just hurry up and let me eat already.

259
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:06,360
Understood.

260
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:08,100
Ready...

261
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:09,700
Purse snatcher!

262
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:14,120
Hey, has the start signal not come yet?

263
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:16,440
This is no time for that!

264
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:18,240
It's a purse snatcher, Officer!

265
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:20,940
What timing!

266
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:26,660
Fine, fine, I'll go, I'll go!

267
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:29,780
Make sure you keep my omelet rice safe!

268
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:32,480
Over there!

269
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:35,800
That one?

270
00:17:36,380 --> 00:17:37,700
Him again!

271
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:39,060
Stop!

272
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:43,600
It's that cop again!

273
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:44,640
Damn it!

274
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:50,400
No good, my vision's getting blurry.

275
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:54,140
What, you followed me?

276
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:57,440
Jumbo omelet rice!

277
00:17:58,440 --> 00:18:00,840
Hold on tight so you don't fall off!

278
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:10,100
We're in the clear once we get this far.

279
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:30,960


280
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:33,120
Too bad, buddy.
Move one step and see what happens.

281
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:34,380
Officer...

282
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,360
Damn it!

283
00:18:44,380 --> 00:18:45,480
You bastard!

284
00:18:47,780 --> 00:18:49,280
You're gonna pay for this!

285
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:54,900
N-no good... my stomach...
I can't get any strength...

