Omelet rice

305
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:24,880
Omelet rice

306
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:27,720
Then remake it right away.

307
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:32,540
That's what that man ordered as a second helping,
and now we've run out of rice.

308
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:35,200
Mine's a second helping!

309
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:37,980
No good, it's hopeless.

310
00:19:37,980 --> 00:19:40,180
The power of electronics...

311
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:51,880
Honestly, how much trouble do you have
to cause people before you're satisfied?

312
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:57,360
You had the peddler's old
lady mind the store for you.

313
00:19:57,830 --> 00:19:59,620
You trashed the police box.

314
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:01,900
You brought a stray dog into the police box.

315
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:03,720
It's truly pathetic.

316
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,200
Chief Ohara.

317
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:07,100
Please let him off with that much, Chief.

318
00:20:07,570 --> 00:20:11,040
He did catch a serial thief while starving,
after all.

319
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,600
Well, I'll give him credit for that much.

320
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:14,620
Excuse me, is anyone here?

321
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:18,300
You're the one from this morning,

322
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:19,820
thank you so much.

323
00:20:20,780 --> 00:20:21,160
Hello.

324
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:23,000
Excuse me!

325
00:20:23,660 --> 00:20:24,040
This is...

326
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:26,620
about the thief that
the senior officer caught.

327
00:20:26,620 --> 00:20:27,640
I see.

328
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:30,780
I didn't get a chance to thank you properly.

329
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:33,760
It's just a small token of my gratitude.
Please, have it.

330
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:37,880
Whoa, that smell is cake!

331
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:41,680
Gimme some of that!

332
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:43,200
Let's eat it

333
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:46,720
Thanks for the food!

334
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:51,200
Senpai

335
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:52,760
He's eating while crying.

336
00:20:52,760 --> 00:20:56,280
Come on, it's just cake.
Does a grown man really have to cry over it?

337
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:59,760
You heartless people could
never understand how I feel.

338
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:04,220
Hey, that's my cake!

339
00:21:04,720 --> 00:21:07,540
And I'm not giving you that Mont
Blanc or my strawberry shortcake either!

340
00:21:07,540 --> 00:21:10,580
You wolfed down the chocolate
gateau And the pear tart.

341
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:14,060
This is all your fault.
We didn't get a single extra one.

342
00:21:14,820 --> 00:21:16,240
That's enough.

343
00:21:17,180 --> 00:21:18,760
Give me some too.

344
00:21:26,060 --> 00:21:29,240
Next up: the return of Hard-Boiled Deka.

345
00:21:33,180 --> 00:21:34,560
It's a Camaro.

346
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:35,920
Could it be that among these...

347
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:40,460
Hoshi from headquarters.

348
00:21:40,460 --> 00:21:44,160
People call me Hard-Boiled Deka.

349
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:45,260
Naturally, you're Hoshi.

350
00:21:55,140 --> 00:21:56,980
Alright, everyone, let's head to the scene.

351
00:21:56,980 --> 00:21:58,980
This has to be hard-boiled, got it?

352
00:22:00,660 --> 00:22:01,820
What is this show?

353
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:04,420
This is just a slice-of-life comedy anime!

354
00:22:04,420 --> 00:22:08,360
At this rate, my hard-boiled
charm won't shine through at all.

355
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:10,040
Here we go again.

356
00:22:13,620 --> 00:22:16,140
This background is no good. Change it.

357
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:26,240
Yes, this is the background
worthy of hard-boiled!

358
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:26,727
Next,

359
00:22:26,777 --> 00:22:30,720
you characters also have to be more realistic,
or it won't work!

360
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:35,300
I-I've become realistic!

361
00:22:35,300 --> 00:22:37,100
This can't be happening...

362
00:22:37,100 --> 00:22:38,140
No way.

363
00:22:38,140 --> 00:22:39,940
What on earth is going on?

364
00:22:39,940 --> 00:22:42,320
We've been turned into a gekiga world again!

365
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:44,560
This is going to be a disaster.

366
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:49,220
Now we're redoing my entrance scene again!

367
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:55,020
Once this starts, it drags on forever.

368
00:22:55,700 --> 00:22:58,040
Looks like there won't
be any One Piece today.

369
00:22:58,620 --> 00:22:59,020
Alright.

370
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:02,520
Right then,
Hard-Boiled Deka entrance, take two.

371
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:03,500
Ready.

372
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:04,240
Action!

373
00:23:15,120 --> 00:23:16,420
It's a Camaro.

374
00:23:16,420 --> 00:23:17,920
Could it be that someone in here...

375
00:23:27,660 --> 00:23:29,280
I'm Hoshi from headquarters.

376
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:33,140
People call me the Hard-Boiled Deka.

377
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:40,700
Why is it ending so suddenly?

378
00:23:40,700 --> 00:23:42,460
It just started!

379
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:44,800
What's going on, Director Takamatsu?

380
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:48,520
Sorry, we have some airtime left over.

381
00:23:48,520 --> 00:23:51,080
We only brought you in to fill time.

382
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:51,980
What?

383
00:23:52,760 --> 00:23:54,380
You can go home now.

384
00:23:55,300 --> 00:23:55,640
No way.

385
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:58,640
This can't be happening.

386
00:23:59,160 --> 00:24:00,440
My big moment...

387
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:04,500
Damn it, I'll definitely be back!

388
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:18,800
Na na na na, na na na na, na na na na

389
00:24:19,960 --> 00:24:24,300
to those who play dumb games over looks

390
00:24:24,300 --> 00:24:27,460
I probably don't want to be like that

391
00:24:27,460 --> 00:24:32,080
if I'm dawdling around the corner

392
00:24:32,080 --> 00:24:34,420
the moon has run away

393
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:38,180
because now isn't everything

394
00:24:38,180 --> 00:24:42,640
don't get too sulky about it

395
00:24:42,640 --> 00:24:46,360
even if you lie or cheat a little

396
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:50,520
sometimes when you're helping someone

397
00:24:50,520 --> 00:24:52,540
Baby, do you know me?

398
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:56,760
toward tomorrow, with a nice spirit

399
00:24:57,820 --> 00:25:04,300
I won't mope, I'll do what I have to do,
with a cute spirit

400
00:25:04,300 --> 00:25:11,360
what's hard to see is that
they want to look that way

401
00:25:11,900 --> 00:25:17,480
isn't it better than a
show that lets you down?

402
00:25:29,660 --> 00:25:30,760
Good morning, Ryogetsu.

403
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:33,200
Now, about your mission this time.

404
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:36,540
This model of the five-story pagoda,
requested by the Police Commissioner General,

405
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:38,880
must be completed by the deadline.

406
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:42,500
Also, this preview will
self-destruct automatically.

407
00:25:43,040 --> 00:25:46,620
Next time: Top Secret Orders,
Mission in the Five-Story Pagoda.

408
00:25:46,620 --> 00:25:48,000
Good luck.

409
00:25:48,800 --> 00:25:51,260
Over there is Kameari.

410
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:54,380
Well, I'm sure it's Kameari.

411
00:25:55,340 --> 00:25:59,300
Everyone, come visit our town!

412
00:26:00,180 --> 00:26:00,920
Thank you.

